From b3983fefbd6d4a34ef07d1f995dbf977ae987d42 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 21:43:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Texture cache: cheaper render target drops and image views

- EDEN_NX2_TC_RT_EVICT walked the LRU list from its oldest end every frame, through the thousands
  of textures older than a few frames, to find the ~15 stale render targets; it now checks a list
  of the transient targets only (kept in JoinImages / DeleteImage).
- Image views asked the driver for the format's depth comparison / min-max support each time
  (~600 views a second); the answer is now kept per format.
- New GPU_PROFILE zones: image delete, framebuffer remove (RemoveFramebuffers walks every
  framebuffer for each deleted image).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HmEAGe4MCAJnHoeqq7Uysk
